==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|noysome||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|noysom}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|noy|some|pos=adjective}} (short for [[annoy]], from {{m|enm|annoien|an(n)oien}}, {{m|enm|enoien}} from {{der|en|xno|-}} {{m|fro|anuier}}, from {{der|en|fro|enuier}} ({{cog|fr|ennuyer}}), from {{der|en|LL.|inodiare||to make hateful}}, from {{m|la|in-|pos=intensive prefix}} + {{m|la|odium||hate}}).<ref>[http://wordsmith.org/words/noisome.html Wordsmith's entry for noisome]</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈnɔɪ.səm/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-noisome.wav|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔɪsəm|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|noi|some}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|literary}} Morally [[hurtful]] or [[noxious]].
# {{lb|en|literary}} Hurtful or noxious to health; [[unwholesome]], [[insalubrious]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:harmful}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|book=Psalms|chapter=91|verse=3|passage=Surely he shall deliuer thee from the snare of the fouler: and from the '''noisome''' pestilence.|}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1912
|author=w:Alexander Berkman
|title=Prison Memoirs of an Anarchist
|chapter=6
|chapterurl={{fullurl:s:Prison_Memoirs_of_an_Anarchist/Part_I/Chapter_6}}
|passage=There is a distinct sense of freedom in the solitude of the night. The day's atmosphere is surcharged with '''noisome''' anxiety, the hours laden with impending terrors. But the night is soothing.}}
# {{lb|en|literary}} Offensive to the senses; [[disgusting]], [[unpleasant]], [[nauseous]], especially having an undesirable [[smell]].
#: {{syn|en|foul|fetid|sickening|nauseating}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Much Ado About Nothing|act=V|scene=i|page=120|passage=Foule words is but foule wind, and foule wind is but foule breath, and foule breath is '''noiſome''', therefore I will depart vnkist.}}
#* {{RQ:Swift Strephon and Chloe|page=8|passage=And then, ſo nice, and ſo genteel; / Such Cleanlineſs from Head to Heel: / No Humours groſs, or frowzy Steams, / No '''noiſom''' Whiffs, or ſweaty Streams, / Before, behind, above, below, / Could from her taintleſs Body flow.}}

